{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CQauEn2YWLYr427z5MHmwU","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-billing-app","number":717,"kind":"pr","title":"(feat) Add delete action for pending bills","state":"merged","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-04-21T06:57:42.000Z","mergedAt":"2026-04-21T20:38:56.000Z","closedAt":"2026-04-21T20:38:56.000Z","url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-billing-app/pull/717","mergeCommit":"db22701b986ae73bc876df2327fa0f82a7fd3ed5","syncedAt":"2026-10-23T18:59:47.249Z","tickets":[],"commits":[{"sha":"db22701b986ae73bc876df2327fa0f82a7fd3ed5","source":"merge-commit-sha","verified":true}],"files":[{"path":"src/bill-history/bill-action-menu.component.tsx","additions":20,"deletions":2},{"path":"src/billing.resource.ts","additions":8,"deletions":0},{"path":"src/index.ts","additions":5,"deletions":0},{"path":"src/invoice/invoice.component.tsx","additions":12,"deletions":0},{"path":"src/modal/delete-bill-confirmation.modal.test.tsx","additions":134,"deletions":0},{"path":"src/modal/delete-bill-confirmation.modal.tsx","additions":98,"deletions":0},{"path":"src/routes.json","additions":4,"deletions":0},{"path":"translations/en.json","additions":6,"deletions":0}],"body":"## Requirements\r\n\r\n- [x] This PR has a title that briefly describes the work done including the ticket number. If there is a ticket, make sure your PR title includes a [conventional commit](https://o3-docs.openmrs.org/docs/frontend-modules/contributing.en-US#contributing-guidelines) label. See existing PR titles for inspiration.\r\n- [ ] My work is based on designs, which are linked or shown either in the Jira ticket or the description below. (See also: [Styleguide](http://om.rs/o3ui))\r\n- [x] My work includes tests or is validated by existing tests.\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nAdds a \"Delete bill\" action for bills in `PENDING` status:\r\n\r\n- New `deleteBill` resource that calls `DELETE /bill/{uuid}?reason=...`\r\n- New `delete-bill-confirmation-modal` prompting for a required deletion reason\r\n- Delete option surfaced from the bill-history overflow menu (gated on `PENDING`) and from the Invoice page action bar (already scoped to `PENDING`)\r\n- On success, refreshes the bill list (bill-history) or navigates back to `home/billing` (Invoice page)\r\n\r\n## Screenshots\r\n<!-- Required if you are making UI changes. -->\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/63b9dfb0-54f6-4f68-b233-997753ed050e\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Related Issue\r\n<!-- Paste the link to the Jira ticket here if one exists. -->\r\n\r\n## Other\r\n<!-- Anything not covered above -->","comments":[{"kind":"review","author":"denniskigen","createdAt":"2026-04-21T10:33:36.000Z","state":"COMMENTED","path":null,"line":null,"body":"Confirmed from the backend source: `DELETE /billing/bill/{uuid}?reason=...` routes to `BillResource.delete` (line 204), which calls `BillService.voidBill`; `voidBill` (line 149) validates the reason but only saves the unchanged bill, no `voided=true`, `voidReason`, `voidedBy`, or `dateVoided` is set. The REST framework doesn't set `voided` before this override runs, and `HibernateBillDAO` still filters `voided=false` by default (line 166), so a \"deleted\" bill remains visible in normal queries.\r\n\r\nContrast: `BaseRestDataResource.delete` (line 168) uses `voidEntity`, and `BillLineItemResource.delete` correctly sets the void fields itself. `BillResource` opts out of both paths.\r\n\r\nThis UI can show a successful delete after a 204 while the bill remains active. Needs a backend fix (or confirmation I'm reading it wrong) before shipping the frontend action.\r\n\r\nAlso, mind adding some screenshots showcasing the new behaviour?"},{"kind":"review_comment","author":"denniskigen","createdAt":"2026-04-21T10:33:36.000Z","state":null,"path":"src/modal/delete-bill-confirmation.modal.tsx","line":16,"body":"Thanks for following the existing modal patterns here, the structure is clean. Could we add a test file for this modal? `delete-line-item-confirmation.modal.test.tsx` would be a good template to mirror, covering the happy path, `responseBody.error.message`, fallback error handling, disabled-state logic, and reason trimming before calling `deleteBill`.\n\nThe PR description says the work is covered by tests or existing validation, but this new modal has its own success/error/control-flow behavior, so a focused test would help catch regressions."},{"kind":"review_comment","author":"denniskigen","createdAt":"2026-04-21T10:33:36.000Z","state":null,"path":"src/modal/delete-bill-confirmation.modal.tsx","line":13,"body":"Small suggestion: since `onMutate` and `onDelete` are both \"run this after a successful delete\" callbacks, could we collapse them into a single `onSuccess?: () => void` prop? One caller can pass `mutate`; the invoice page can pass the navigation callback. The modal does not need to know which kind of success follow-up it is running, and this keeps the prop surface smaller."},{"kind":"review_comment","author":"denniskigen","createdAt":"2026-04-21T10:33:36.000Z","state":null,"path":"src/bill-history/bill-action-menu.component.tsx","line":17,"body":"Minor: `BillActionMenu` is currently only rendered from `bill-history.component.tsx` when `currentBill?.status === BillStatus.PENDING`, so this `isPending` check is redundant for the current call site. I'm fine leaving it as defense-in-depth if we expect this menu to be reused elsewhere, just flagging the duplication."},{"kind":"review","author":"denniskigen","createdAt":"2026-04-21T10:34:40.000Z","state":"COMMENTED","path":null,"line":null,"body":""},{"kind":"review_comment","author":"denniskigen","createdAt":"2026-04-21T10:34:40.000Z","state":null,"path":"src/modal/delete-bill-confirmation.modal.tsx","line":33,"body":"Tiny wording nit: could we drop \"has been\" and use `'Bill deleted successfully'`? That matches the existing delete idiom in the codebase (`lineItemDeleteSuccess` is `'Bill line item deleted successfully'`), which this modal is otherwise modeled on. Reads a touch crisper in the snackbar too."},{"kind":"review_comment","author":"denniskigen","createdAt":"2026-04-21T10:34:40.000Z","state":null,"path":"translations/en.json","line":42,"body":"If we tighten the subtitle, this would become `\"billDeleteSuccess\": \"Bill deleted successfully\"` for consistency with `lineItemDeleteSuccess` just below."},{"kind":"issue_comment","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-04-21T12:06:27.000Z","state":null,"path":null,"line":null,"body":"> Confirmed from the backend source: `DELETE /billing/bill/{uuid}?reason=...` routes to `BillResource.delete` (line 204), which calls `BillService.voidBill`; `voidBill` (line 149) validates the reason but only saves the unchanged bill, no `voided=true`, `voidReason`, `voidedBy`, or `dateVoided` is set. \r\n\r\nSo Claude always flags this, but the voided properties get set by an interceptor in core for void functions, so they do get saved, and I double checked on the database too, and it gets saved. This is probably butchering the correct explanation, but\r\n\r\n> voidBill is intercepted by openmrs-core's RequiredDataAdvice AOP (RequiredDataAdvice.java:161), which invokes BaseVoidHandler to set voided, voidReason, voidedBy, and dateVoided before the service method body runs. The save(bill) call persists those fields.\r\n\r\nAs to this -\r\n\r\n> HibernateBillDAO still filters voided=false by default (line 166)\r\n\r\nsince we haven’t had a requirement so far to need to be able to see voided bills, we haven’t supported it, so we currently don’t have a way to be able to fetch voided bills\r\n\r\n> This UI can show a successful delete after a 204 while the bill remains active.\r\n\r\n\r\nI’ve verified that it doesn’t. I had a screen recording but forgot to attach it, lol, sorry. I’ve updated the PR description with the recording\r\n"},{"kind":"review","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-04-21T12:15:37.000Z","state":"COMMENTED","path":null,"line":null,"body":""},{"kind":"review_comment","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-04-21T12:15:37.000Z","state":null,"path":"src/modal/delete-bill-confirmation.modal.tsx","line":16,"body":"fair, will add a test mirroring the line-item one."},{"kind":"review","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-04-21T12:15:39.000Z","state":"COMMENTED","path":null,"line":null,"body":""},{"kind":"review_comment","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-04-21T12:15:39.000Z","state":null,"path":"src/modal/delete-bill-confirmation.modal.tsx","line":13,"body":"yeah makes sense, will collapse to `onSuccess`."},{"kind":"review","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-04-21T12:15:41.000Z","state":"COMMENTED","path":null,"line":null,"body":""},{"kind":"review_comment","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-04-21T12:15:41.000Z","state":null,"path":"src/bill-history/bill-action-menu.component.tsx","line":17,"body":"yeah, leaving it as defense-in-depth — keeps the component safe to reuse without relying on the caller to gate it."},{"kind":"review","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-04-21T12:15:43.000Z","state":"COMMENTED","path":null,"line":null,"body":""},{"kind":"review_comment","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-04-21T12:15:43.000Z","state":null,"path":"src/modal/delete-bill-confirmation.modal.tsx","line":33,"body":"Done!"},{"kind":"review","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-04-21T12:15:45.000Z","state":"COMMENTED","path":null,"line":null,"body":""},{"kind":"review_comment","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-04-21T12:15:45.000Z","state":null,"path":"translations/en.json","line":42,"body":"Done!"},{"kind":"review","author":"denniskigen","createdAt":"2026-04-21T12:38:02.000Z","state":"APPROVED","path":null,"line":null,"body":"LGTM. Thanks, @NethmiRodrigo!"}],"nextOffset":null,"truncated":[]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f48b8c2c-f736-437f-a7e1-0b9e312d5cd4","